WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:16.216
( whirring )

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:08.201
( window opening )

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:10.570
Shuttle Pilot: Might want to
take a step back, Captain!

00:01:12.805 --> 00:01:16.843
Oh, by the way, I'm a huge fan.

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:19.712
- Closing blast shields. 
- No, no! NO-- aah!

00:01:19.812 --> 00:01:21.214
 Shuttle Marmota,
 you are cleared to dock.

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:24.617
( laughs )
What an idiot!
Boom! We're here.

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:29.222
You like bratwurst?
My uncle has bratwurst,
like, a restaurant.

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:30.723
I was thinking maybe you and me,

00:01:30.823 --> 00:01:32.559
we could go
grab a couple of brewskis

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:35.361
and pop out there.

00:01:35.461 --> 00:01:38.231
Welcome aboard
the Invincible II.

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:40.400
Glad to have you here.
Took you long enough.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.735
Let me give you the grand tour
before we embark.

00:01:42.835 --> 00:01:45.338
( glitching )
This is my pride and joy. 
My baby.

00:01:47.439 --> 00:01:49.409
( distorted )
A baby always remembers

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:51.411
its father.

00:01:51.511 --> 00:01:54.614
 ( distorted echoes )
 Father, father, father...

00:01:57.449 --> 00:01:58.885
First stop, the--

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:01.654
the heart and soul of the--

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:04.591
I've yet to meet a problem that
can't be solved with explosives.

00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:05.792
And speaking of explosives--

00:02:08.627 --> 00:02:13.766
( distorted chatter )
All will be consumed by
darkness.

00:02:13.866 --> 00:02:16.603
( slowed )
Hi, Captain!

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:18.037
Celci:
Where are you going, Captain?

00:02:18.137 --> 00:02:22.442
Ms. Whitacre: Do you think she
 had  the right idea, Captain?

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:26.913
 Did she give up
 or did she move on?

00:02:27.013 --> 00:02:29.682
 All a matter
 of perspective, I suppose.

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:33.686
 ( echoing laughter )

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:38.791
Come on, slowpoke.

00:02:38.891 --> 00:02:42.729
 ( overlapping echoes )

00:02:47.299 --> 00:02:49.802
 ( echoes continue )

00:02:53.772 --> 00:02:56.442
All that's left now...

00:02:59.511 --> 00:03:01.314
...is for you to say the word.

00:03:01.414 --> 00:03:03.249
Try not to get them
too excited, Captain.

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:06.753
I know how your speeches
can get people riled up.

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:11.958
( laughing, grunting )

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:14.827
Captain, why does
this seem familiar?

00:03:14.927 --> 00:03:16.896
Eh? Aah!

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:20.833
 ( music playing )

00:03:20.933 --> 00:03:23.836
Narrator:
 And so our intrepid Captain
 falls headlong

00:03:23.936 --> 00:03:26.973
 into the spiraling chaos
 of dimensional calamity,

00:03:27.073 --> 00:03:30.510
 heralding the beginning
 of the end.

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:32.612
 My goodness,
 what an adventure.

00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:35.515
 I swear, this story
 never ceases to amaze me.

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:37.850
 By the way,
 it's good to see you again.

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:40.687
 Or for the first time,
depending on your past choices.

00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:43.456
 Either way,
 I'm sure we'll meet again
 for the first time

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:46.993
 in the very near future
 and/or somewhat distant past.

00:03:47.093 --> 00:03:51.698
 Should this not prove
 to be the end of all reality,
 which it almost certainly is,

00:03:51.798 --> 00:03:53.900
 it would be my great pleasure
 to guide you

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:57.537
 through my own universe
 should the opportunity arise.

00:03:57.637 --> 00:03:59.372
 Which doesn't seem likely
 to happen at this juncture,

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:01.374
 but when thinking
 in infinites,

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:06.579
 unlikely is just certainty
 waiting for its turn.

00:04:12.851 --> 00:04:14.721
- ( running footsteps )
- ( knocking on door )

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:16.889
What's wrong, sport?

00:04:16.989 --> 00:04:19.726
Bless my stars,

00:04:19.826 --> 00:04:21.928
was it the nightmare
about the spaceship again?

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:25.798
That one just keeps coming back,
doesn't it?

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:27.900
Well, I know just the thing
that's going to cure that--

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.569
another story.

00:04:29.669 --> 00:04:31.904
All right,
let's see what we got here.

00:04:32.004 --> 00:04:34.574
Ugh, maybe
a little too grisly.

00:04:34.674 --> 00:04:36.909
Uh, read that one
too many times.

00:04:37.009 --> 00:04:38.044
Nah.

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:40.280
Not in the mood.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:41.447
Eh, not today.

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:47.587
Why don't you decide, huh?

00:04:47.687 --> 00:04:50.056
You could read
a nice romance story.

00:04:50.156 --> 00:04:52.592
That'd be fun.
Or a horror story.

00:04:52.692 --> 00:04:54.560
I know how much
you love scary stories.

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:56.596
But it might give you
a few more nightmares,

00:04:56.696 --> 00:04:59.065
so you could go romance.

00:04:59.165 --> 00:05:01.768
It'll be a little silly
and more than a little sappy,

00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:04.771
but it might be just the thing
to kick you right back to sleep.

00:05:04.871 --> 00:05:06.773
Well, whatever you choose,
I can guarantee

00:05:06.873 --> 00:05:09.442
it's going to come with
a big ol' hug free of charge.

